.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET_VERIFY_RESULT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get_verify_result
.Nd get result of peer certificate verification
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft long
.Fo SSL_get_verify_result
.Fa "const SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_get_verify_result
returns the result of the verification of the X509 certificate presented
by the peer, if any.
.Fa ssl
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn SSL_get_verify_result
can only return one error code while the verification of a certificate
can fail because of many reasons at the same time.
Only the last verification error that occurred during the processing is
available from
.Fn SSL_get_verify_result .
.Pp
Sometimes there can be a sequence of errors leading to the verification
failure as reported by
.Fn SSL_get_verify_result .
To get the errors, it is necessary to setup a verify callback via
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_verify 3
or
.Xr SSL_set_verify 3
and retrieve the errors from the error stack there, because once
.Xr SSL_connect 3
returns, these errors may no longer be available.
.Pp
The verification result is part of the established session and is
restored when a session is reused.
.Sh BUGS
If no peer certificate was presented, the returned result code is
X509_V_OK. This is because no verification error occurred, it does
however not indicate success.
.Fn SSL_get_verify_result
is only useful in connection with
.Xr SSL_get_peer_certificate 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The following return values can currently occur:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It X509_V_OK
The verification succeeded or no peer certificate was presented.
.It Any other value
Documented in
.Xr openssl-verify 1 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_set_verify_result 3 ,
.Xr SSL_get_peer_certificate 3 ,
.Xr openssl-verify 1
